    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d29">

                <pb facs="0139" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg35"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Mizner</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 21,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Adee informs Mr. Mizner that the Pacific Mail Company has been advised that
                    the Guatemalan Government has confiscated the arms carried by the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Colima</hi>, and instructs him to pretest and demand
                    restoration. Asks him if he has received Department’s telegrams of 19th and 20th
                    instant.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
